WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
So Hank, today, uh, Nat Wolff and I are just going to go to the woods and do a Question Tuesday...

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.660
That sounded weird! [Nat]: A little creepy.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.720
[Nat]: Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday! [John]: It's Question Tuesday,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.700
the day that we answer real questions from real Nerdfighters.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.480
I'm here with Nat Wolff, who's playing Isaac in the movie, and I'm going to ask him some questions,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.920
[Nat]: I look here? [John]: That you guys submitted from Twitter. Yeah, right inside the.. it's right in there.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.240
All right Nat, your first question:

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.720
"Is Shailene Woodley a good kisser?"

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.800
[Nat]: nshwgb ahb uhh... Was that question meant for me?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.580
[John]: Awkward panda. [Nat]: oh, oh, oh, oh. [John]: yeah, mm

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.660
[Nat]: Uh, I wouldn't know. I- I- sadly, Isaac doesn't get to kiss, uh, Hazel.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.980
[John]: Yeah, have you guys read the book?! [Nat]: Yeah, but... [John]: Doesn't happen.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.960
What part of the book are you most excited to see in the movie?

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.180
[Nat]: I'm excited to see, uh, I think... I did the trophy scene, I think that went well.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.520
[John]: I'm excited to see all the scenes that don't have Isaac in them

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.200
[Nat]: Hmm, not as much for me.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.260
[John]: Who's the funniest person on the Fault In Our Stars set? [Nat]: One, two, three.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.020
[Both]: Me.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.920
[John]: It's definitely me. [Nat]: It's me. [John]: It's me. [Nat]: It's me. [John]: I know I'm...

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.940
[Nat]: Okay, it's John. [John]: You're second, you're second, but it's a distant second.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.000
How true to the book is the movie? [Nat]: Very true. I think it's because people -

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.160
You trying to get me out of this camera angle, John?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.640
[John]: Hahahha how- how true to the book IS the movie, Nat?

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:10.180
[Nat]: I think people are so in love with this book and it's so realistic already, we- there's barely anything that anybody had to change.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.000
[John]: But I can't help but notice that you don't have BLONDE HAIR. [Nat]: Ugghh escept for my blonde hair!

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.940
[John]: As the author of the book, I just want to say that that stuff doesn't matter to me at all.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.040
Uhm, maybe I'll make a Tumblr post about why it doesn't matter to me and link to it in the video info below.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.120
[Nat]: Yeah, so guys, for all the tweets about me not being blonde: I'm sorry.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.620
[John]: (Laughs) It's not- it's not his fault, he was born that way.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.660
[Nat]: Neither of my parents have blonde hair. I just couldn't control it. They were- you know, blame them.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.340
[John]: If you could only watch one more movie in your life, Nat, what would it be?

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.620
[Nat]: Uhh, it would probably be Taxi Driver, I think Taxi Driver is probably my favourite movie of all time.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.980
[John]: For me, it would definitely be The Fault In Our Stars.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.580
[Nat]: I meant The Fault In Our Stars. [John]: Yeah.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.800
What's it been like hanging out with, uh, actual teen cancer survivors?

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.740
[Nat]: It was- it was overwhelming. I went to, uh, a hospital and, uh, I talked to them and

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.940
you know, you start off asking them questions about their disease and how they cope with it

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.680
and about 5 minutes in you're talking about movies and TV shows and music, just like with anybody else.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.820
[John]: Right. [Nat]: And you realise they're just normal kids who are just going through a really lame situation.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.400
[John]: Have you seen me cry on set at all?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.220
[Nat]: Yeah I have. John cries... at a good meal.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.140
[John]: Nat, this is your second movie with Josh Boone, [Nat]: Yeah. [John]: as a director. What do you think of that guy?

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.460
[Nat]: Ugh, screw him, man. [John]: Yeah, he's kind of lame. [Nat]: Josh Boone is like one of my

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:22.920
best friends in the world, honestly. Hopefully I'll be working with him for, you know, the rest of my career.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.100
[John]: Yeah, that's how I feel about Nat. I want to work with him a lot. But not-

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.760
[Nat]: I want to work with John for the rest of my... [John]: Not on movies, you know? Just like...

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.300
[Nat]: Just like, work on little projects. We could build a house together.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.820
[John]: What's it like playing a blind person?

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.380
[Nat]: When I'm doing the scenes blind, I really can't see anything.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.140
Uhm, eh- I put stuff over my glasses, or I'm wearing these contacts that make it so I can't see anything

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:43.200
And, uh, it's almost freeing, because you become real- you lose all self-conciousness.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.460
Physically, I watched a lot of videos online of blind people, I met with this guy named Ethan.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:54.320
Uhm, and... I, you know, watched Scent Of A Woman. [Both laugh]

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.780
So I got some of those speeches memorized, you know?

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.520
[John]: So you got the Al Pachino blind strength? [Nat]: Yeah, it's like: "I'm in the dark, Charlie!"

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.800
[John laughs] [Nat]: "I'm in the dark!" So I'm trying to work that into the movie somehow.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.960
"I'll take a flaaame-thrower to this place!"

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.020
[John]: Give me some Ansel. [Nat]: Uh, hey, uh, what are you talking about? No, ummm...

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.800
Im having a good time today. Here's my John.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.600
[John]: Hahahahha!

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.160
(Whispering): We're being quiet 'cause we got in trouble.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.940
Do you have a favorite book? [Nat]: I mean, my favourite book of all time is The Catcher In The Rye,

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:23.160
and also 'cause like Hazel, I think I read it at a really important time in my life,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.440
when a book can mean that much to you.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.420
[John]: The Catcher In The Rye is also my- probably my favorite book.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.700
That must be why we're buddies. [Nat]: Is that really? [John]: Yeah. [Nat]: Really your favorite book? [John]: Yeah.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.860
I made- I'll send you my videos I made about it. Favorite Beatle? [Nat]: Paul. [John]: Favorite color?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.640
[Nat]: Blue. [John]: Meh, see mine are- mine are John and green.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:43.020
[Nat]: Honestly, John is... Now as I get older, becomes more my favorite. I mean, it's hard. John and Paul...

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.080
[John]: Do you find yourself coming 'round to green at all? As a color?

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.560
[Nat]: Not at all. [John]: Damn it!

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.020
One, two, three [Both]: Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.320
[John]: Let's do it one more time, where it's a little less lame. A little- little better than that.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.840
One, two, three. [Nat]: Hank!

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.740
[John]: One, two, three. [Both]: Hank, I'll see you on Friday. [John]: That was good!

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.580
[Nat]: Yeaaah! Finally! [John]: Up top.

